WEBVTT

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.880
Excuse me. My name is Richard Stewart.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.540
I'm a photographer.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.960
May I take a picture of you and your little boy?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:40.820
What's it for?

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.660
It's for a book.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.980
You're writing a book?

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.860
It's a book of pictures.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.870
I call it Family Album, U.S.A.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.560
Oh, that's a nice idea.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.500
Well, it's fine if you take our picture.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.800
I'm Martha Vann.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.980
Thank you. I appreciate your help.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.280
I'm Richard. What's your name?

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:57.880
Gerald.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.360
How old are you, Gerald?

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:01.440
And where do you live?

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.880
We live in California.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.080
Well, welcome to New York.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.690
OK, just a second.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.520
I'm almost ready here.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.460
Oh, please.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:26.620
Hold Gerald's hand, please. Great!

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.000
Now point to the buildings.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.300
Terrific!

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.040
Thank you, Gerald.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:47.840
Oh, my pleasure.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.260
We'll be looking for your book.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.380
Thanks again.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.760
Oh, you're welcome.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.720
Hey, let me take your picture!

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:02.600
Wonderful. Please.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.720
Are you from New York?

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.180
No, I'm from Greece.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.120
I'm an exchange student.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.160
When did you come here?

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:17.840
Three months ago.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.820
Your English is very good.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.240
Thanks.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.160
I studied English in school.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.060
Would you like some coffee?

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.480
No, thank you.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.880
Tell me about your book.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.080
Oh, it's not finished yet,

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.100
but I have some of the pictures.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.180
Would you like to see them?

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.420
Yes. I'd like that.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.480
It's an album of pictures of the United States:

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.320
the cities, the special places, and the people.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.860
And these are pictures of people working:

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.760
Oh, this is my father. He's a doctor.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.820
This is my mother.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.910
What's her name?

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:18.530
Ellen.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.440
My younger brother, Robbie.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.820
He goes to high school.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.180
This is my sister Susan.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.440
She works for a toy company.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.820
Here's my grandfather. He lives in Florida.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.500
And this is my wife Marilyn.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.880
Oh, she's very pretty.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.380
Thanks. And what about your family?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.340
They are in Thessaloniki.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.480
That's a large city in northern Greece.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.920
But now I'm living in the Bronx.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.200
With a Greek-American family?

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.500
No. Hispanic.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.120
Oh no! It's five thirty.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.260
Will you excuse me?

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.250
I have to meet my wife.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.900
Thanks for your help.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.950
And good luck! I've got to go.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.220
By the way, I'm Richard.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:13.880
What's your name?

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:14.420
Alexandra.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.040
Bye-bye, Alexandra. Thanks.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:23.840
Bye-bye. Richard! Richard! You left your bag!
